From 44cdded94f582e40a0e1fa54f95379bd3435776d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/51] B70-IP-K8: int8-dot attn2 faster than bf16 (aligned
 gathers, int8 launch regions)

Root cause of round 1 (int8 Q.K slower than bf16): the inline int8 cell pitch
is 520 B, so Triton could not prove any alignment of a gathered K/V row and
emitted byte loads, and the int8 tiles kept the bf16 launch shape (BLOCK_N 32,
one subgroup) whose fp32 per-tile partials dominate prefill.

- ALIGN8 (host-checked by i8dot_align8: V = K + head_dim + 4 in the same cell,
  8-B aligned K rows): multiple_of(8) cell offsets and V addressed from the K
  pointer, so gathers vectorize.
- Own launch regions sparse_attn2_i8_{decode,prefill} (I8DOT=1: BLOCK_N 64,
  2 subgroups, grf auto) and sparse_attn2_i8pv_* (I8DOT=2: BLOCK_N 128,
  4 subgroups). These shapes crash IGC 2.41.5 in bf16 (SIGFPE guard kept for
  bf16) and compile in int8; halving/quartering tiles cuts the partial traffic.
- Tile q stride taken from the int8 Q actually passed; warmup compiles the
  int8 regions with the runtime ALIGN8.

B70 card 2, TP2 12q/1kv, width 2051, kernel-only (XPU graph): prefill 4096
rows bf16 14.99 ms -> I8DOT=1 11.94, =2 11.15; decode 64 rows 0.298 -> 0.216 /
0.170; decode 8 rows 0.103 -> 0.065 / 0.043. TP1: prefill 30.14 -> 23.85 /
22.14.
